Quiver: persist each bundle's ingestion time in the segment manifest and hand
it to the pipeline as the pdata's `ingestion_time`.

The WAL already records a bundle's ingestion time (and WAL replay preserves
it), but a finalized segment dropped it, and the durable buffer delivered
every bundle with a default context. An exporter behind the buffer could only
use its own receive time, which changes on every redelivery: a NACK's retry,
and a replay after a restart. This keeps the first ingestion time:

- quiver: `ManifestEntry` gains an optional `ingestion_time_ns`, written as a
  nullable Int64 manifest column `ingestion_time_ns` when any bundle has one
  (the `byte_count` pattern: legacy segments read back as `None`, and older
  readers ignore the column); `ReconstructedBundle::ingestion_time()`.
- otap: `Context` / `OtapPdata` gain `ingestion_time()` /
  `set_ingestion_time()`, kept by `clone_detached`.
- core-nodes durable buffer: `convert_bundle_to_pdata` sets it from the
  bundle.

The payload bytes are unchanged. Upstreamable as is.

